    "body": "\n\n## Overview\n\nFixes #61172. The Anthropic entrypoint's system conversion silently drops any non-`text` content block (e.g. an `image` block) both in the top-level `system` field (`_convert_system_message`) and in inline system messages (`_extract_system_text`). The OpenAI endpoint already warns about this (#34072) but the Anthropic path never did, so unsupported blocks vanished without a trace.\n\n## Claims\n\n- Emit a `logger.warning_once` naming the dropped content type when an unsupported Anthropic system content block is ignored, mirroring the OpenAI endpoint's wording.\n- Keep the existing behavior of ignoring unsupported blocks (backward compatible) — only the warning is added.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `ruff check` and `ruff format` clean.\n- Behavior-level verification running the real conversion functions against the real request model passes 6/6 checks (warning + preservation + no-warning boundaries).\n- New regression tests cover top-level and inline image blocks (warning emitted + text preserved), plus text-only / string / billing-header cases that must NOT warn.\n\n## Details\n\nRoot cause: `_convert_system_message` / `_extract_system_text` drop any content block whose type is not `text` without notifying the caller, so callers can pass e.g. `system: [{\"type\":\"image\",...}]` and have it silently ignored. The fix keeps the drop (backward compatibility) but surfaces it with a once-per-type warning.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [ ] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n\n",
